From b6c226130cd7410071bd7bdc9108d4c17318d147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuk3s <44327449+nuk3s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:14:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kv-offload): check each disk slot's header and checksum
 on load

Upstream base: the patch applies to local-inference-lab/vllm at
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the 702 patches of
spark-ds41f-1120 (candidate-62, 0001 to 0829) and patches 9030 to 9033
of this series.

Rationale: a read that returned the wrong bytes was served to the model
with no error, whether the cause was a misdirected or lost write, a torn
slot, media corruption, or a slot that was never written. Under
O_DIRECT, when the padded slot has room for 32 bytes (a DeepSeek-V4.1
slot has 1,536 bytes of padding), the store thread now writes a header
after the block bytes. The header holds a magic number, a version, the
checksum kind, the slot id, a generation, and a checksum of the block
bytes; the generation is the slot's store count in this process, which
the worker keeps in a per-slot array. The slot id catches a misdirected
read, the generation catches a stale slot, and the checksum catches
changed bytes. The load thread checks the whole header after preadv and
before any DMA, and a mismatch raises DiskTierError(EBADMSG), which takes
the fault path of the previous patch: the load fails as a cache miss and
the tier degrades. The new kv_connector_extra_config key disk_checksum
takes "crc32" (the connector's default), "sum64" (a 64-bit word sum), or
"none". DiskBackend.init defaults to "none", so direct callers keep the
layout without a header.

Quality implications: a correct read gives the same output as before.
The generation array costs 2 x 8 bytes of memory for each slot on each
rank. The checksum adds CPU time to every load and store; its cost on
the ARM cores of a GB10 was not measured alone, and "sum64" is the
cheaper option.

Tests: tests/v1/simple_kv_offload/test_ds41_tier_faults.py checks round
trips with crc32 and with sum64. A byte flipped in the data or in the
header of the file fails the load before any DMA, and the GPU block
stays untouched. A lost write, made by restoring the previous generation
in the file, and a slot that was never written also fail the load. A
4096-byte block leaves no room for a header and turns the check off. On
the CPU path the offload suite passed 146 tests, with 2 CUDA-only modules
skipped. On DGX Spark hardware the patch ran only as part of the whole
series.

Upstream status: the patch is proposed to spark-ds41f in
experiments/2026-11-22-kv-disk-tier and has not been submitted to
local-inference-lab/vllm.
